WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:03.036
First of all, an absolute
pleasure, because you've helped

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.739
put Lao cuisine on the map.

00:00:05.805 --> 00:00:07.941
I'm dying to get to
understand the Lao cuisine.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:11.211
Right.

00:00:14.514 --> 00:00:15.215
GORDON RAMSAY: Yes.

00:00:18.184 --> 00:00:18.918
Wow.

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:19.719
[interposing voices]

00:00:19.786 --> 00:00:20.854
That's incredible.

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:24.557
What is he doing over
there, that crazy man?

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:26.292
GORDON RAMSAY: I mean, not
the safest place to fish.

00:00:26.359 --> 00:00:27.093
JOY NGEUAMBOUPHA: Yes.

00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:28.194
Because very strong water.

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:29.028
Yes.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:31.398
So that the fish more tasty.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:32.999
Wow.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.401
Wow.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.935
So by fighting the current, they
get a little bit more tastier.

00:00:36.002 --> 00:00:37.370
More tasty, more--
more exercise.

00:00:37.437 --> 00:00:38.405
GORDON RAMSAY: Wow.
More exercise.

00:00:38.471 --> 00:00:39.539
More exercise, yeah.

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:40.540
And so there's a big
difference between fish

00:00:40.607 --> 00:00:41.808
being caught down here--
- Yeah.

00:00:41.875 --> 00:00:43.343
--than there is over the
other side of the rapids.

00:00:43.410 --> 00:00:44.043
Yes.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.145
It's just so dangerous.

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.479
He's almost like on
the edge of that rock.

00:00:46.546 --> 00:00:47.747
Yeah.

00:00:47.814 --> 00:00:48.548
Me?

00:00:48.615 --> 00:00:49.349
Yeah.

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.184
It's dangerous, right?

00:00:51.251 --> 00:00:53.420
[music playing]

00:00:53.486 --> 00:00:54.220
Not really.

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:55.021
Not really?

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.790
No.

00:00:56.856 --> 00:00:58.591
GORDON RAMSAY: Yeah,
I'd beg to differ.

00:00:58.658 --> 00:01:02.462
Khone Falls are the
widest in the world.

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:05.799
And 2.5 million gallons of
water crash over these rocks

00:01:05.865 --> 00:01:06.566
every second.

00:01:09.502 --> 00:01:12.405
I was hoping for lunch, but
this wasn't what I had in mind.

00:01:17.177 --> 00:01:19.145
What in the [bleep]
are we doing?

00:01:19.212 --> 00:01:19.946
Seriously?

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:21.014
Yeah.

00:01:21.080 --> 00:01:22.582
You sure this will
take my weight, Joy?

00:01:22.649 --> 00:01:23.850
Yeah.
I'm sure, yeah.

00:01:31.291 --> 00:01:34.627
[bleep] Where are we going?

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:36.262
Man!

00:01:36.329 --> 00:01:38.498
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Local fisherman Mr. [inaudible]

00:01:38.565 --> 00:01:40.400
has been risking his life--

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:45.505
sorry, catching these prized
Mekong fish for decades.

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:50.677
[bleep] [bleep] Slippery bank.

00:01:50.743 --> 00:01:54.647
Joy, these fish better
taste [bleep] delicious.

00:01:54.714 --> 00:01:55.715
This is crazy.

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.983
GORDON RAMSAY (VOICEOVER):
Traditional cast

00:01:57.050 --> 00:02:00.553
net fishing has been practiced
for thousands of years.

00:02:00.620 --> 00:02:01.754
Elbow.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:03.089
GORDON RAMSAY
(VOICEOVER): But I've just

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:04.724
minutes to get the hang of it.

00:02:04.791 --> 00:02:05.525
[non-english speech]

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.526
Hold.

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:09.028
Happy, ready?

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.163
This is not a good idea.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:15.602
Yes.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:17.003
JOY NGEUAMBOUPHA: [inaudible]

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:22.342
Oh, come on.

00:02:22.408 --> 00:02:23.776
[bleep]

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:27.647
Oh, [bleep].

00:02:27.714 --> 00:02:29.516
I tell you what, they
make it look so easy.

00:02:29.582 --> 00:02:32.452
But there is nothing
easy in this.

00:02:32.519 --> 00:02:34.320
That's an edgy place to fish.

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.524
It's the force of that
water inches away from you.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.527
And one slip and you're gone.

00:02:40.593 --> 00:02:41.528
Joy, this time--

00:02:41.594 --> 00:02:42.462
This time?

00:02:42.529 --> 00:02:43.663
--we're going to
catch something.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:44.464
Yes.

00:02:44.531 --> 00:02:47.200
Here we go.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:48.134
Wow.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.235
[clapping]

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:54.807
Pull it in?

00:02:54.874 --> 00:02:55.608
Yeah.

00:02:55.675 --> 00:02:57.010
Nothing.

00:02:57.076 --> 00:02:59.145
There's got to be an easier way
of catching fish here, surely.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.683
JOY NGEUAMBOUPHA: Come on.

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:04.450
Oh!

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:11.824
GORDON RAMSAY: [bleep].

00:03:11.891 --> 00:03:12.592
Nothing.

00:03:14.627 --> 00:03:15.328
What?

00:03:19.766 --> 00:03:22.569
So you're telling me it's
not the right time of day.

00:03:22.635 --> 00:03:25.538
Holy, [bleep] [bleep].

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:28.508
Joy, there's no joy in this.

00:03:28.575 --> 00:03:31.010
Thankfully, Mr. [inaudible]
takes pity on me

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:34.180
and kindly shares
his morning catch.

00:03:34.247 --> 00:03:35.882
Oh, my god.

00:03:35.949 --> 00:03:37.283
And was that here?

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.084
JOY NGEUAMBOUPHA: Yes.

00:03:38.151 --> 00:03:39.719
Look at those beauties.

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:41.588
They're gorgeous, right?

00:03:41.654 --> 00:03:43.022
Let's go and eat some
before we get killed.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.090
Yeah, yeah.

